  "emoji": "🧭",
  "summary": "Ask for and give simple directions: right, left, straight ahead, near and far, and the first, second and third street.",
  "intro": "To find your way you need يَمِينًا (to the right), يَسَارًا (to the left) and إِلَى الْأَمَام (straight ahead). You also learn the ordinal numbers: الشَّارِع الْأَوَّل (the first street), الشَّارِع الثَّانِي (the second street). An ordinal is an adjective, so it comes after the noun and agrees with it: الْبِنَايَة الثَّالِثَة (the third building).",
  "objectives": [
    "Stop someone politely and ask the way",
    "Give directions with right, left and straight ahead",
    "Use the ordinals first to fifth with masculine and feminine nouns",
    "Say whether a place is near or far"
  ],
